Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

**The user's role for me:** assistant and coworker on a technical assessment. I must remind them of anything they're missing, help investigate and define decisions, and follow the assessment PDF (`C:\Users\Quijote\Downloads\Technical assessment -Frontend.pdf`).

**What the assessment asks for:**
- A multi-country (Colombia/Chile) car insurance quote wizard: Angular 21+ and Strapi 5+, with the form fields and plans configurable from Strapi.
- An agentic flow with versioned subagents, skills, a CLAUDE.md, ADRs, specs, review evidence, traceability, FLOW.md and README.
- Unedited session logs in `ai-logs/`.
- Weighting: 65% agentic flow, 35% app.

**Chosen approach:**
- Claude Code plus Spec Kit (modified), with 3 human gates:
  - Gate 1: spec plus clarify;
  - Gate 2: plan;
  - Gate 3: handoff review.
- Autopilot runs in between.

**Current work:**
- US-00 (country selection) is past Gate 1 and in Gate 2 (plan).
- The user rejected the Gate 2 choices and asked for interactive canvas mockups of:
  - the selection screen: two big country buttons on the same line, with "Continuar" centered below;
  - the wizard header, both options.
- No E2E for this screen.
- The plan is not approved yet ("no yet, check what I told you").

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

**Stack:**
- Angular 22.3:
  - standalone, zoneless, signals, `@if`/`@for`;
  - Vitest, ESLint, strict TypeScript, Playwright.
- Strapi 5.63: TypeScript, SQLite.
- Node 24 locally and Node 22 in Docker.
- Docker Compose with an nginx same-origin proxy (`/api` → `cms:1337`; `/uploads` planned).

**Spec Kit:**
- Version 1.4.4.dev0, installed via uv with `--integration claude --script sh`.
- Skills: speckit-specify, clarify, plan, tasks, analyze, implement.
- Sequential feature numbering. No extensions.yml and no hooks, so the branch is created manually.

**Agentic flow:**
- Constitution, plus CLAUDE.md as the global context file.
- Subagents:
  - cms-developer (sonnet);
  - frontend-developer (sonnet);
  - e2e-tester (sonnet, conditional on approved candidates);
  - code-reviewer (opus).
- Skills:
  - autopilot;
  - angular-conventions;
  - strapi-conventions;
  - ui-ux-guidelines (Sura-inspired tokens, Figtree from the Google Fonts CDN).
- `.claude/settings.json`:
  - allow: the flow's commands;
  - ask: npm install, git push/reset/rebase;
  - deny: reading `.env`; editing docs/user-stories, the constitution and ai-logs.

**Flow steps:**
- 0a constitution;
- 0b human story intake;
- 1 specify;
- 2a clarify, 2b Gate 1;
- 3a plan, 3b Gate 2;
- 4a tasks, 4b analyze (automatic, saved to analysis.md);
- 5 implementation waves;
- 6 conditional E2E;
- 7 verify;
- 8 review (review.md, 2 rounds);
- 9 commit (`Refs: US-XX`);
- 10 Gate 3 (`Gate 3: Approved — date` in review.md);
- 11 QA.

**Traceability:**
- `US-XX` and `FR-XXX` IDs.
- `**Status**: Approved (Gate N) — date`.
- Gate 1 corrections in Clarifications, Gate 2 in plan Revisions, Gate 3 as new tasks.

**ADR 0001 (multi-country, Proposed; becomes Accepted at Gate 2):**
- Country, FormField and Plan are collections; FormField and Plan relate to Country.
- Draft/publish is on all three.
- Path prefix `/co/quote`; `/` is the selection screen.
- Active is enforced server-side.
- One sessionStorage session per tab.

**ADR 0002 (agentic workflow, Accepted and amended):** Spec Kit with 3 gates, plus the analyze amendment.

## 3. Files and Code Sections

**Repo:** `C:\Users\Quijote\Documents\insurance-multiregion-app`
- Remote: `https://github.com/quijotex/insurance-multiregion-app.git`.
- `main` has been pushed.
- The current branch `001-us-00-country-selection` is not pushed.

**Governance and flow files:**
- **`.specify/memory/constitution.md`:** the user's constitution, word for word. Deny-protected.
- **`CLAUDE.md`:**
  - repo structure, including specs with analysis.md;
  - verification commands;
  - stack rules;
  - Plan Phase Additions: E2E candidates, design options from ui-ux-guidelines, ADRs, Revisions;
  - an "Asking the Human" section: always AskUserQuestion, one question per call, recommended option first, echo the answer in text;
  - traceability rules, security and hygiene.
- **`FLOW.md`:**
  - Mermaid diagram and steps table;
  - governance, including settings.json;
  - agents table;
  - a journal of adjustments: 0b intake, conditional e2e, reviewer, Gate 3 plus Revisions, permissions, analyze 4b, AskUserQuestion fix;
  - the no-AI points.
- **`.claude/agents/*.md`:** cms-developer, frontend-developer (skills: angular-conventions, ui-ux-guidelines), e2e-tester, code-reviewer (all three skills).
- **`.claude/skills/autopilot/SKILL.md`:**
  - reads the constitution, CLAUDE.md and specs;
  - verifies Gate 2;
  - generates tasks with `[P]`, `[CMS]`/`[FE]` and US/FR tags;
  - analyze rules:
    - CRITICAL/HIGH findings in tasks.md: fix and rerun, max 3;
    - findings needing a spec or plan change: stop and ask;
    - MEDIUM/LOW: keep and continue;
  - waves with subagents, then verify (max 3);
  - commits with Refs;
  - conditional e2e;
  - review loop of 2 rounds;
  - handoff summary.
- **`.claude/skills/angular-conventions`, `strapi-conventions`, `ui-ux-guidelines`:** project knowledge, including design tokens, for example:
  - `--color-brand:#0033a0`, `--color-action:#2d6df6`;
  - `--color-cta:#e3e829` with `--color-on-cta:#26328c`;
  - `--color-accent:#00aec7` (decorative only).
- **`.claude/settings.json`:** the allow/ask/deny rules described above.

**Docs:**
- `docs/adr/0000-template.md`.
- `docs/adr/0001-multi-country-content-strategy.md`, updated during this plan:
  - Country fields include icon (media), order and active;
  - countries query: `GET /api/countries?fields[0]=name&fields[1]=code&sort=order:asc&populate[icon][fields][0]=url&populate[icon][fields][1]=alternativeText`;
  - active enforced by the controller;
  - `/uploads/` proxy;
  - two switches (published and active);
  - unknown/inactive prefixes redirect to `/` with a message;
  - one session per tab, with a confirmation;
  - preselection of the last visited country.
- `docs/adr/0002-agentic-workflow-spec-kit-and-human-gates.md`.
- `docs/user-stories/README.md`.
- `docs/user-stories/US-00.md`: the user created it; it is deny-protected.

**Other files:**
- `README.md`: wizard steps table (US-00 to US-03), quick start, tests, structure; the admin section says "To be completed with US-00".
- `ai-logs/README.md`.
- `docker-compose.yml`: cms and frontend services, dev-only secret defaults.
- Dockerfiles, `frontend/nginx.conf` and `frontend/proxy.conf.json`.
- `frontend/playwright.config.ts`: webServer array of Strapi develop (`/_health`) and ng serve, plus an `E2E_BASE_URL` override.
- `frontend/playwright.docker.config.ts`.
- `frontend/package.json` scripts: typecheck, test `--watch=false`, e2e, `e2e:docker`, verify.

**US-00 spec folder (`specs/001-us-00-country-selection/`):**
- **`spec.md`:**
  - Status: Approved (Gate 1) — 2026-11-22;
  - 5 clarifications:
    1. select, then Continue;
    2. preselect the last visited country;
    3. a header "Cambiar país" control on every step;
    4. wizard shell with a step 1 placeholder;
    5. a new-tab link opens directly; a same-tab link confirms first;
  - FR-001 to FR-012;
  - the ADR conflicts section.
- **`checklists/requirements.md`:** all items pass.
- **`research.md`, R1 to R8:**
  - R1: the controller enforces active;
  - R2: icon is a media field, with SVGs drawn for the project; the Public upload permission must be verified;
  - R3: `/uploads` proxy;
  - R4: guard redirects to `/?unavailable=code`, with a lower-case canonical redirect;
  - R5: `quote-session` key `{countryCode, data}`;
  - R6: native `<dialog>`;
  - R7: bootstrap grants the Public find permission, seeds CO (order 1), CL (order 2) and an inactive PE (order 3), and creates the admin from `ADMIN_EMAIL`/`ADMIN_PASSWORD`;
  - R8: only US-00 fields for now.
- **`data-model.md`, `contracts/countries-api.md`, `contracts/routes.md`, `quickstart.md`.**
- **`plan.md`:**
  - Status: Draft;
  - summary, technical context, constitution check, structure, ADR changes;
  - design options:
    - selection screen: A tiles, B list (recommended), C split hero;
    - header: A navy top bar (recommended), B country line;
  - E2E-1 and E2E-2 marked Rejected (Gate 2), with the note "No E2E for this story";
  - test plan;
  - Revisions: "2026-11-22 — Gate 2, round 1 (not approved)", recording the interactive mockup request, the two side-by-side buttons with Continue centered, and the E2E rejection.

**Memory:** `C:\Users\Quijote\.claude\projects\C--Users-Quijote-Documents-insurance-multiregion-app\memory\`
- `export-session-logs-reminder.md`
- `ask-questions-with-dialog.md`
- `MEMORY.md`

## 4. Errors and fixes

- **PDF reading:** no pdftoppm was available, so I extracted the text with pdftotext.
- **Spec Kit:** `--ai` is not a valid option, so I used `--integration claude`. Agent detection failed, so I added `--ignore-agent-tools`.
- **Bash heredoc failure:** writing FLOW.md through a heredoc failed with "unexpected EOF", so I used the Write tool instead.
- **CRLF warnings:** I added `.gitattributes` with `* text=auto eol=lf`.
- **Cross-platform env vars:** setting an environment variable in an npm script isn't portable, so I created a separate `playwright.docker.config.ts`.
- **User-stories file:** I refused to create `docs/user-stories/US-00.md` because the deny rule blocks it and intake is human-only. The user created it.
- **Clarify question not seen:** I wrote the first clarify question in prose before wrap_up, and the user didn't see it ("ask me clearly… take notes"). Fix:
  - an "Asking the Human" rule in CLAUDE.md;
  - a FLOW.md journal entry;
  - a memory entry;
  - all later questions asked through AskUserQuestion.
- **Emoji flag in header Option B:** I replaced it with "[flag]".

## 5. Problem Solving

- The Docker stack was verified: health returns 204, the frontend returns 200, the SPA fallback works, and the `/api` proxy reaches Strapi. The smoke e2e test passed through `e2e:docker`.
- Q5 answer: the browser keeps sessionStorage per tab, so the new-tab case needs no extra code.

## 6. All user messages

1. Shared the PDF and asked me to read it in full, extract every detail and share my thoughts ("you won't allow me to forget them… help me investigate and define").
2. Gave the flow plan:
   - they will export logs to `ai-logs/` and want a reminder;
   - Claude Code plus Spec Kit with two gates;
   - the constitution, autopilot skill and CLAUDE.md content;
   - "set up Spec Kit, CLAUDE.md, the required stack, and our agentic workflow".
3. "Yes, commit it".
4. Answers 1–7: "make me a proposal" for subagents; accepted the review; create FLOW.md; ADRs at the Plan gate; IDs; proposed a CLAUDE.md draft; FLOW must start from the functional user story.
5. E2E agent only for critical flows approved at the plan step; design options at the plan step from a UI/UX skill; research sura.com; rest OK; asked to proceed with the remaining items.
6. "Two caveats ok. Let's use it Figtree from Google Fonts cdn, and a light-weight fallback. Go ahead and create the skill".
7. Multi-country ADR content (Strapi and Angular parts, rejected options), with "Don't change a lot my writing style".
8. ADR fixes 1–10: add the requested changes; for item 5, asked whether the concern is valid; delete option a and keep only b; redirect; "why do you ask? I think so".
9. "No catalog… keep it simple. But mention what we found, the limits and what would need a developer"; add item 10; the redirect goes to the sessionStorage country, falling back to the first in the list.
10. "Commit it".
11. ADR 0002 content: Spec Kit and 3 human gates.
12. Corrections: "the constitution serves" → "the constitution.md serves"; keep the considered options; three gates; Revisions for Gate 2.
13. "No, we haven't set up yet Strapi account, what do we need to be fully ready?"
14. Answers: follow the admin recommendation; Docker is on; add permissions ("we can't have these stops besides the approved one by the flow"); rename to main; remote is `https://github.com/quijotex/insurance-multiregion-app.git`; add the README; e2e environment now; "got it" on logs.
15. "Push it".
16. Add analyze after step 4, with no extra human gates, and adjust the docs; add a country selection screen as the first story; "Docker engine is up".
17. Dialog answers: always show the selection screen; ID US-00.
18. Pasted US-00 and asked me to create the file and run /speckit-specify. I refused because of the deny rule.
19. "You were right, I had forgotten it. It is already there. run /speckit-specify".
20. Dialog Q1: Select, then Continue.
21. "Hey, but ask me clearly, I don't see the questions and options, and take notes of this, because is an improvement for future runs".
22. Dialog Q2: preselect the last visited country.
23. Dialog Q3: header control on every step.
24. Dialog Q4: wizard shell plus placeholder.
25. Dialog Q5: "If the links opens in a new tab… your recommended option… same tab… option two… take both cases into account".
26. Gate 1 dialog: approved the spec.
27. "Start the plan".
28. Gate 2 dialog answers:
    - Selection: "No, I want to see the interactive design on your canvas no like that. And position the two country buttons on the same line, bigger and below, on the center the continue button".
    - Header: "same as before, I want the interactive design".
    - E2E: "No e2e for this screen".
    - Approve: "no yet, check what I told you".

## 7. Pending Tasks

- Show the interactive canvas mockups (`show_widget`):
  - the selection screen with two large country buttons on one line and "Continuar" centered below;
  - both wizard header options, A (navy top bar) and B (country line), interactive.
- Then ask again through AskUserQuestion: the header pick, any selection-screen tweaks, and approval of the plan and the ADR 0001 changes.
- On approval:
  - update plan.md's design options with the chosen designs;
  - set Status `Approved (Gate 2) — date` and ADR 0001 to Accepted;
  - commit with `Refs: US-00`;
  - run /autopilot if the user agrees: tasks → analyze → waves → verify → no E2E → review → commit → Gate 3.
- Not committed yet: the plan artifacts, the ADR 0001 edits and the plan Revisions.
- Later stories: US-01, US-02, US-03 (verbatim intake by the user).
- At the end, remind the user to export conversations to `ai-logs/`.

## 8. Current Work

Gate 2 for US-00. After the user's rejection:
- I updated `plan.md`: E2E candidates marked Rejected, plus the Revisions entry for round 1.
- I called `mcp__visualize__read_me` (modules mockup and interactive) to prepare the interactive mockups.

The mockup design follows ui-ux-guidelines:
- Figtree font;
- navy `#0033A0`; action blue `#2D6DF6`;
- yellow CTA `#E3E829` with navy `#26328C` text;
- pill buttons; cards with 16px corners;
- Spanish copy: title "¿Dónde quieres asegurar tu carro?", button "Continuar", header "Cambiar país".
- Countries Colombia and Chile with flag placeholders. Selecting a country enables Continuar; the last visited country is preselected.
- Header options A and B are both interactive; for example, clicking "Cambiar país" can show the confirm dialog mockup.

Visualize constraints:
- No emoji; use Tabler icons.
- Use a faux-viewport div for modals; no `position: fixed`.
- Brand colors are acceptable inside a mockup surface, but the outer container stays transparent.
- End the text before the `show_widget` call with a sentence saying the drawing follows.

## 9. Optional Next Step

Call `show_widget` with an interactive mockup of the selection screen and both header options, per the user's latest instruction:
- "No, I want to see the interactive design on your canvas no like that. And position the two country buttons on the same line, bigger and below, on the center the continue button"
- "same as before, I want the interactive design"

Then ask through AskUserQuestion (per the CLAUDE.md "Asking the Human" rule): which header option, whether the selection design is right, and whether to approve the plan and the ADR 0001 changes. Record the answers in plan.md Revisions and Design options before committing.

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\Users\Quijote\.claude\projects\C--Users-Quijote-Documents-insurance-multiregion-app\d03f5fd3-f739-4643-9962-49381622158d.jsonl
Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with "I'll continue" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.

The messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them.

tools.description:
Open the Browser pane: pass `url` to open a browser tab at a URL (no dev server needed — use this for external sites, staging, docs, or your deployed app), OR pass `name` to start a dev server from .claude/launch.json.

Start a dev server by name from .claude/launch.json. If .claude/launch.json doesn't exist, create it first with this format:
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "<unique-name>",
      "runtimeExecutable": "<command>",
      "runtimeArgs": ["<args>"],
      "port": <port>
    }
  ]
}
Set "runtimeExecutable" to the command (e.g. "npm"), "runtimeArgs" to the arguments (e.g. ["run", "dev"]), and "port" to the server port. An optional "url" (http/https) opens the preview there instead of http://localhost:<port>. A localhost "url" must be just the server's origin — no path or query, matching the entry's port — for example "https://localhost:8443" or "http://app.localhost:3000"; to show a specific page, navigate after the preview opens. Non-localhost URLs may carry paths and are subject to the user's permission and the organization's browsing policy. A configuration with "url" and no command attaches to an already-running server. Only include servers you actually need to preview. Reuses the server if already running. ALWAYS use this instead of Bash for running servers. If the deliverable is already published as an Artifact, update the Artifact instead of starting a server to show it.

